m1	464,205,1556,418		The once-accented octave: a treble staff with seven semibreves rising stepwise from middle c on a ledger line, lettered beneath c', d', e', f', g', a', b'.
m2	464,500,1556,702		The twice-accented octave: a treble staff with seven semibreves rising stepwise from the third space to above the staff, lettered beneath c'', d'', e'', f'', g'', a'', b''.
m3	464,1010,1556,1222		The great or 8-foot octave: a bass staff with seven semibreves rising stepwise from two ledger lines below the staff, lettered beneath C, D, E, F, G, A, B.
